    id: "econ-2017-hl-sa-q8", topicId: "economics-3-1", conceptId: "conflicting-policy-objectives",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2017 HL Section A Q8",
    questionText: "Explain how the following Government policy objectives may conflict with each other. Economic growth versus Balance of Payments equilibrium: Economic growth versus a Just Social Policy:",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"12 + 5","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 17,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Each conflict explained", marks: 17, contextNote: "Both conflicts: the first correct response 12 marks, the second 5. For the second the scheme also gives an example: To achieve a just social policy the government may impose high taxes on the high-income earners and transfer this income to those on social welfare/High taxes could force these people out of the economy and so seriously impede the effort to achieve economic growth.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":12,"options":["Economic growth versus Balance of Payments equilibrium — Economic growth means more employment and more money circulating in the economy. As Ireland has a high MPM this will automatically cause an increase in imports which could result in a Balance of Payments deficit.","Economic growth versus a Just Social Policy — Economic growth tends to benefit incomes of the better off. The benefits of economic growth may not be equitably distributed across the economy. Social policies such as taxation etc. are needed to redistribute benefits of economic growth."],"perOptionSteps":[12,5]} },
    ],
