    id: "econ-2018-hl-sb-q7-b", topicId: "economics-3-4", conceptId: "regulating-the-banking-sector",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2018 HL Section B Q7(b)",
    questionText: "Outline the economic advantages of effective regulation of the banking sector. Your answer should include advantages for citizens and advantages for the banking industry.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"7 + 6 + 6 + 6","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 25,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Two advantages for citizens and two for the banking industry", marks: 25, contextNote: "A minimum of two for citizens and two for the banking industry. The scheme prices the four on one ladder, not by side: the first credited 7 marks (3 + 4), the other three 6 each (3 + 3).", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":4,"perOption":7,"options":["Citizens — Provide protection to depositors / consumers To ensure sound and solvent financial institutions giving depositors confidence that their deposits and investments are safe. /customers have confidence in the financial system. Avoid consumers being over-charged e.g. trackers mortgage scandal.","Citizens — May help consumers make better financial decisions Some consumers can make poor financial choices e.g. take on too much debt or choose products that do not match their needs. Therefore, they need protection through regulation.","Citizens — Confidence in banking sector / economic growth By regulating the banking sector consumers will have confidence in the banking sector. It may encourage greater savings. A stable banking sector will facilitate economic growth.","Citizens — Secure employment By ensuring that the banking sector is secure it may mean stability in this sector and thus ensure that jobs are secure.","Citizens — Benefits for taxpayers/less need for government intervention If banks are stable and promote savings and investment, then they become more profitable, providing more funds for government services. It also means that there is reduced risk of tax payer funds being needed (for possible bailouts).","Banking sector — To avoid reckless lending Proper regulation should ensure that banks, which engaged in excessive risk-taking and reckless property-related lending, which resulted in Irish borrowers borrowed too much in the past, should not re-occur. •","Banking sector — To maintain stability in the financial system / provide investor confidence To foster a stable / healthy financial system. Regulation will ensure the financial sector will operate efficiently and public confidence will be restored. •","Banking sector — Less prone to shocks / need for government intervention and decision making It will help to ensure that what happened in 2008 should not re-occur and therefore there will be less shocks to the financial system reducing the need for government intervention. •","Banking sector — To reduce macro-economic instability When banks were left to their own devices they loaned excessively in good times and little in bad times. Regulation ensures that this boom/bust cycle is controlled. Strong financial institutions are necessary for an economy."],"perOptionSteps":[7,6,6,6]} },
    ],
