    id: "econ-2021-hl-sa-q4-a", topicId: "economics-2-2", conceptId: "demerit-goods",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2021 HL Section A Q4(a)",
    stem: "In budget 2021, the price of a 20 pack of cigarettes rose from €13.50 to €14.00. Cigarettes are classed as ‘Demerit Goods’ and as such their purchase constitutes a market failure.",
    questionText: "Explain your understanding of the economic term Demerit Goods.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"4 + 3","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 7,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Demerit goods are goods whose positive effect is overestimated by consumers and which have negative effects which consumers possibly underestimate or are unaware of. Demerit goods usually also have negative externalities i.e., they have negative effects on third parties not involved in the consumption of the good.", marks: 7, contextNote: "Explain the term, 7 marks (4 + 3): a good whose benefit consumers overestimate and whose harm they underestimate, and which usually carries negative externalities.", openList: true },
    ],
