    id: "econ-2021-hl-sa-q7-b", topicId: "economics-3-1", conceptId: "disadvantages-of-a-budget-surplus",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2021 HL Section A Q7(b)",
    questionText: "Explain the economic disadvantages for a government in achieving a budget surplus.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2 @ 3","answer":2,"ofParts":6,"perPart":3}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A disadvantage of a budget surplus — any two", marks: 6, contextNote: "Two disadvantages, 3 marks each.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":3,"options":["Rise in conflicting expectations When citizens observe the budget surplus they may demand improvements in state services e.g. health services; education provision etc. However, the demands/expectations made on the government may conflict.","Public Sector Workers When public sector workers see this budget surplus they may see it as an opportunity for wage negotiations. Workers may thus demand pay increases and /or an increase in the level of the workforce.","Tax burden Taxpayers who feel that they are paying too much tax may feel aggrieved. They may demand reductions in their tax / improved equity in the tax system.","Government financial planning The surplus may indicate that the planning by the government was not sufficiently accurate at budget preparation time.","Opportunity costs of a surplus The budget surplus may have been achieved by the reduction of expenditure on services within the country. Thus, essential services such as health, education etc may have deteriorated.","Difficulties in the Social Partnership model The existence of the budget surplus may cause discontent within society. Citizens may feel that certain sectors are benefiting more from government policies. May prove difficult in approving national agreements."]} },
    ],
