    year: 2021, level: "higher",
    paperFileid: "LC034ALP000EV",
    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2021 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2021-hl-q11-c-ii", topicId: "economics-1-5", conceptId: "internal-economies-of-scale",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2021 HL Q11(c)(ii)",
    stem: "Boeing and Embraer entered potential merger talks in 2019. If a merger were to occur between Boeing and Embraer it is likely they would benefit from Internal Economies of Scale.",
    questionText: "Outline possible Internal Economies of Scale which could arise for Boeing and Embraer if this merger were to occur.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"3 @ 6","answer":3,"ofParts":8,"perPart":6}, totalMarks: 18,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "An internal economy of scale from the merger — any three", marks: 18, contextNote: "Three economies, 6 marks each (2 + 4).", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":3,"perOption":6,"options":["Labour economies: there may be increased specialisation of workers on their specific tasks. This may lead to increases in productivity of the firm which will help reduce costs.","Managerial economies: only the best managers from both firms will be kept on board reducing the costs of administrative / unproductive staff.","Purchasing economies: the scale of production of the overall firm will now be larger and thus they may be able to purchase raw materials on a larger scale. Bulk buying may lead to lower per unit costs.","Technical economies: as the firm’s merge, they may be able to pool resources to afford the most advanced technology which will reduce production costs per unit.","Economies in use of raw materials: the firm can use the same basic components on all its aircraft and so there is less chance of resources being wasted, helping to reduce costs.","Economies in distribution: post-merger the firm may have more enterprises in more locations which may result in result in reduced transportation costs for per unit of raw materials and finished products.","Marketing economies: the firm can spread the cost of marketing across a wider range of output thus reducing the cost on a per unit basis. A single specialist marketing team can be better utilised across a wider range of aircrafts.","Financial economies Larger firms may have access to a greater range of finance options than a smaller firm and are more likely to be able to borrow at lower rates of interest hence reducing production costs. Some capital investment is only suitable for high levels of output."]} },
    ],
