    questionText: "Firms in Perfect Competition are said to be Price-Takers. On the diagrams below label and illustrate: (i) What happens to the market equilibrium as more firms enter the market? (ii) What happens to the individual firm’s price as more firms enter the market? Explain each of your diagrams below. In the long run only the most efficient firms will survive. Explain this statement.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal","notation":"15","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 15,
