    year: 2022, level: "higher",
    paperFileid: "LC034ALP000EV",
    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2022 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2022-hl-q12-c-ii-for", topicId: "economics-1-3", conceptId: "the-case-for-more-data-centres",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 HL Q12(c)(ii) — for",
    stem: "Analysis has shown that demand for electricity from data centres could account for 29% of all demand for electricity in Ireland by 2028. (A data centre is a remote place, with many servers, used for the storage, processing and distribution of information.)",
    questionText: "Discuss one reason why the Irish government should grant planning permission to additional data centres in Ireland and one reason why the government should not grant planning permission. Reason for:",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"1 @ 4","answer":1,"ofParts":5,"perPart":4}, totalMarks: 4,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A reason for granting planning permission — any one", marks: 4, contextNote: "One developed reason for, 4 marks (2 + 2). The question asks for one reason each way and the scheme prices each 4.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":4,"options":["Supports technological industry in Ireland. Ireland has become increasingly technologically advanced in recent years. Continued growth and development in these areas is essential to sustainable economic growth in Ireland.","Supports employment in the tech industry/STEM. STEM jobs represent on third of the Irish job market. Allowing additional development within this industry will continue to provide additional jobs for people in this sector.","Source of government revenue. Data centres are in huge demand and thus highly profitable. The Irish government stands to benefit from additional taxes on earnings from these companies and their employees.","Investment is an injection into the circular flow of income. Additional investment into the circular flow of income should be encouraged as it may have a multiplier effect, leading to further growth in the economy.","May encourage further FDI. Some MNCs may consider locating in Ireland if they see a growth in the availability of these data centres here."]} },
    ],
