    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2022 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2022-hl-q12-c-ii-against", topicId: "economics-1-3", conceptId: "the-case-against-more-data-centres",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 HL Q12(c)(ii) — against",
    stem: "Analysis has shown that demand for electricity from data centres could account for 29% of all demand for electricity in Ireland by 2028. (A data centre is a remote place, with many servers, used for the storage, processing and distribution of information.)",
    questionText: "Discuss one reason why the Irish government should grant planning permission to additional data centres in Ireland and one reason why the government should not grant planning permission. Reason against:",
