    id: "econ-2022-hl-q16-b-ii-citizens", topicId: "economics-0-2", conceptId: "low-carbon-strategy-citizens",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 HL Q16(b)(ii) — Irish citizens",
    stem: "The UN Secretary-General said the Working Group's report for sustainability was a code red for humanity. The alarm bells are deafening, and the evidence is irrefutable.",
    questionText: "Suggest strategies that could be employed by the Irish government and Irish citizens to aid with the transition to a low carbon economy. Irish Citizens:",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"1 @ 7","answer":1,"ofParts":3,"perPart":7}, totalMarks: 7,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A strategy for Irish citizens — any one", marks: 7, contextNote: "One developed strategy for Irish citizens, 7 marks (4 + 3). The question asks for both actors and the scheme prices each 7.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":7,"options":["More ethically aware consumption of goods. If consumers are more particular about the products they purchase and are more aware of the production processes involved in producing these products, they can become an active part of reducing carbon consumption in Ireland.","Concerted efforts to reduce consumption of goods which are harmful to the environment. Some consumers are happy to consume products regardless of their environmental impact. If this pattern can be changed it will speed up this process. E.g. swapping to electric vehicles.","Increase efforts to recycle products. Efforts to make the life of a product longer and keep it out of landfill help to reduce carbon emissions into the environment. Recent trends such as upcycling have been helpful on this front."]} },
    ],
