    id: "econ-2022-hl-deferred-sa-q5-b", topicId: "economics-3-5", conceptId: "benefits-of-rural-broadband",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2022 HL Section A Q5(b) — Deferred sitting",
    stem: "Ireland has one of the fastest growing data centre markets in Europe. Currently, most data centres in Ireland are located in Dublin with others in Cork, Limerick and Galway. (A data centre is a remote place, with many servers, used for the storage, processing and distribution of information.)",
    questionText: "The €5.7 bn rural broadband scheme is far behind its initial roll out target. The National Broadband plan remains a focus of the Irish government. Outline two benefits of the rural broadband scheme to rural communities.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2 @ 4","answer":2,"ofParts":6,"perPart":4}, totalMarks: 8,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A benefit of the rural broadband scheme — any two", marks: 8, contextNote: "Two benefits, 4 marks each (2 + 2).", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":4,"options":["Improved standard of living: the NBP will ensure that all people and businesses have access to high-speed broadband, no matter where they live or work. Once completed, all parts of Ireland will have access to a modern and reliable broadband network which should result in a more efficient service, enhanced entertainment options leading to an improved standard of living.","Option of remote/tele working – the rural broadband scheme should give rural residents the option of remote/tele working which could lead to productivity gains.","Equitable service for all - the National Broadband Plan (NBP) is the government's plan to deliver high speed broadband services to all businesses, farms and households in Ireland. It will ensure that everyone in Ireland will have equal access to a high-speed broadband service.","Protection of the environment – the scheme should help to mitigate emissions with a rise in remote/tele working which should help with the sustainable development goals.","Education – With improved access, learning outcomes should be enhanced through engaging interactive activities.","Viable rural communities – the availability of broadband should allow the continued existence of vibrant rural communities / increased economic activity / reduced pressure in urban areas."]} },
    ],
