    id: "econ-2023-hl-q14-a-iii", topicId: "economics-3-2", conceptId: "types-of-unemployment",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2023 HL Q14(a)(iii)",
    questionText: "Describe two types of unemployment giving examples to support your answer.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2 @ 7","answer":2,"ofParts":5,"perPart":7}, totalMarks: 14,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A type of unemployment, with an example — any two", marks: 14, contextNote: "Two types, each described with an example, 7 marks each.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":7,"options":["Structural unemployment: This occurs when there is a mismatch between the skills of those that are unemployed and jobs available. E.g. jobs becoming obsolete due to new technology.","Frictional unemployment: This occurs due to frictions in the labour market. The transition between jobs usually takes time. E.g. a person is between jobs.","Seasonal unemployment: This is unemployment that can occur at certain times of the year. E.g. a person working in tourism may find themselves unemployed in the winter months in Ireland.","Cyclical unemployment: When there is a downturn or contraction in the economy, demand for goods or services tends to fall leading to unemployment. E.g. people lost their jobs during the Covid-19 pandemic.","Institutional unemployment: relates to unemployment created by institutional arrangements e.g. high minimum wage."]} },
    ],
