    id: "econ-2024-hl-q11-b-i", topicId: "economics-3-0", conceptId: "the-multiplier-and-what-it-means",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2024 HL Q11(b)(i) — calculation",
    stem: "It has been estimated that in the Irish economy: MPT = 0.22, MPM = 0.30 and MPC = 0.6.",
    questionText: "Based on the information stated above and using an appropriate formula, calculate the value of the multiplier in the Irish economy and explain the economic meaning of your answer. Show all your workings. Do the calculation.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"12","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-answer", kind: "point", verbatim: "Answer = 1.08", marks: 12, contextNote: "MPS = 1 − 0.6 = 0.4. Multiplier = 1 ÷ (MPT + MPM + MPS) = 1 ÷ (0.22 + 0.3 + 0.4) = 1 ÷ 0.92; or 1 ÷ (1 − (0.6 − 0.22 − 0.3)) = 1 ÷ 0.92. The scheme prints 1.08; 1 ÷ 0.92 = 1.086956…, which rounds to 1.09.", openList: true },
    ],
