    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2024 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2024-hl-q15-c-i", topicId: "economics-4-1", conceptId: "reasons-to-join-the-eu",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2024 HL Q15(c)(i)",
    stem: "In 2023, Ireland celebrated its 50th anniversary of its membership of the EU. Other countries like the Ukraine and Moldova wish to join the EU.",
    questionText: "Give two reasons why countries wish to join the EU.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"6 + 4","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A reason to join the EU — any two", marks: null, contextNote: "Two reasons: the first correct one 6 marks and the second 4.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":6,"options":["Access to the single market - the EU's main economic engine is the single market. It enables most goods, services, money and people to move freely throughout most of the continent. The EU is the largest trade bloc in the world. It is the world's biggest exporter of manufactured goods and services, and the biggest import market for over 100 countries. This is an attractive proposition for indigenous businesses that would have a bigger market for their produce.","Ease of movement / travel / work – with EU membership, it is much easier to move around Europe – all EU citizens have the right to study, work or retire in any EU country. As an EU national, for employment, social security and tax purposes, every EU country is required to treat you exactly the same as its own citizens.","Provision and protections of citizens’ rights - The Treaty on the European Union gives EU citizens and legal residents a wide range of rights, enacted in EU law across many fields.","Access to financial funds / improvements in standard of living – it is usual for new members of the EU to receive funds to enable new members help develop their infrastructure and provide services comparable with established members. Thes should improve citizens standard of living.","International diplomacy & development - EU countries acting in unison have much more of a voice on the world stage than 27 nations of varying size acting separately. Taken together, the EU institutions and national governments are the world’s leading donor of development assistance and work collectively to promote good governance, fight hunger and preserve natural resources.","Democratic society / structures - Moldova wants EU membership for many reasons but currently a major reason is protection against a possible threat from Russia and its authoritarian regime."],"perOptionSteps":[6,4]} },
    ],
