    questionText: "Outline the overall trend in Ireland’s general government debt, as shown in the diagram above, using data from the chart. Indicate which overall trend you are commenting on by ticking ( ✓) the relevant box: Government debt as a % of GNI* or Government debt as a % of GDP Answer for: DEBT AS A % OF GDP.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"6","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-trend", kind: "point", verbatim: "Government Debt as a % of GDP: There is a downward trend in government debt as a percentage of GDP. • In 2021, it was 54%. • It dropped to 44% in 2022 and remained at 44% in 2023. • Forecasts predict a slight decline to 42% in 2024 and 39% in 2025. • It falls by 15 percentage points over the course of the chart.", marks: 6, contextNote: "The ticked series: state the downward trend and support it with two distinct figures or the overall fall, as the scheme requires (“Downward + Reference to two distinct figures or overall percentage decrease”).", openList: true },
    ],
