    id: "econ-2026-hl-sa-q6-b", topicId: "economics-3-5", conceptId: "benefits-of-theme-parks-to-a-country",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2026 HL Section A Q6(b)",
    stem: "Ireland’s main theme park is Emerald Park in Co. Meath.",
    questionText: "Outline two economic benefits of the operation of theme parks within a country.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2 @ 3","answer":2,"ofParts":8,"perPart":3}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A benefit to the country — any two", marks: 6, contextNote: "Two benefits, 3 marks each.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":3,"options":["Creates employment – theme parks create direct employment through ride operations, maintenance, administration, catering, entertainment etc. They also create indirect employment in hotels, transport and retail services linked to visitor demand.","Increases invisible exports / spending by tourists – overseas tourists who visit theme parks, spend money on rides, food, and accommodation. Such spending by foreign tourists is treated as an invisible export, which increases national income / improves the balance of payments.","Increases tax revenues – theme parks generate tax revenue through VAT on ticket sales and purchases, PAYE from employees, and corporation tax on company profits.","Increases regional economic development – theme parks located outside major cities can stimulate economic activity in surrounding areas by attracting visitors and encouraging local business growth.","Multiplier effect – spending by visitors and employees circulates through the economy, creating further income within the economy.","Develops infrastructure – the establishment of theme parks may lead to improvements in roads, transport links and public services in the surrounding region.","Supports local businesses – nearby hotels, restaurants, shops and transport providers benefit from increased visitor numbers.","Attracts foreign direct investment if foreign-owned – international firms investing in theme parks bring capital investment into the country and may transfer skills and expertise from abroad."]} },
    ],
