    id: "econ-2026-hl-q11-c-i-meaning", topicId: "economics-1-4", conceptId: "interpret-income-elasticity",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2026 HL Q11(c)(i) — explanation",
    stem: "When Cian’s weekly income is €400 he goes to the gym twice a week. When his income increases to €500 he goes three times a week.",
    questionText: "Assuming Cian pays per gym visit, calculate Cian’s income elasticity of demand (YED). Show all your workings and explain your answer. Write the explanation.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"5","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 5,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-meaning", kind: "point", verbatim: "The sign is plus therefore the good is a normal good. There is a positive relationship between the income of the consumer and quantity demanded. The absolute value is 1.8. The demand is income elastic as its YED is greater than 1. The percentage change in the quantity demanded is greater than the percentage change in the consumer’s income. This is a luxury good.", marks: 5, contextNote: "Explain both the sign (normal good) and the size (income elastic, a luxury); 5 marks for the explanation.", openList: true },
    ],
